// lichen sprigs...
ctx.stroke();

if (this.terrain) ...
```
Replace all with:
```
const stamp = performance.now();
if (this.plantLayerDirty || stamp - this.plantLayerStamp > 90) {
  this.paintPlantLayer(sim);
  this.plantLayerStamp = stamp;
}
if (this.plantLayer.width) {
  ctx.drawImage(this.plantLayer, 0,0,this.plantLayer.width,this.plantLayer.height,0,0,w,h);
}
```
Then terrain.

Note: `performance.now()` in a snapshot renderer is fine. The `plantLayerStamp` starts 0, so it draws.
- The `paintPlantLayer` sets `plantLayerDirty=false`.
- On resize, dirty true.
- If the sim is paused, the layer still refreshes every 90ms because the stamp check doesn't know it's paused. It redraws the same field every 90ms; okay but unnecessary. Could check sim.tick, but fine. The cost ~9k checks. 
- The layer includes dots at CSS coords; the DPR transform. Good.

